/*
Problem: Broken Calculator (LC 991)
Topic: Greedy

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Instead of transforming startValue
into target, work backwards from the
target.

Allowed forward operations:

• Multiply by 2
• Subtract 1

Reverse operations:

• If target is even:
      Divide by 2.

• If target is odd:
      Add 1
      (reverse of subtracting 1).

Keep doing this until target becomes
less than or equal to startValue.

If target is smaller than startValue,
the only way is to subtract 1 from
startValue repeatedly.

--------------------------------------------------

Time: O(log target)

Space: O(1)

--------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int brokenCalc(int startValue, int target) {

        int count = 0;

        while(target > startValue) {

            if(target % 2 == 0)
                target /= 2;
            else
                target++;

            count++;
        }

        // Remaining operations are decrements
        count += startValue - target;

        return count;
    }
};
